  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_6' aria-label=\" State of Odisha & Ors. versus Managing Committee of Namatara Girls High School pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('6','2026','2026_3_103_112','2026INSC148'); ><font size='4'> <strong>STATE OF ODISHA & ORS.<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>MANAGING COMMITTEE OF NAMATARA GIRLS HIGH SCHOOL </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 3 S.C.R. 103</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 148</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000652026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : DIPANKAR DATTA, SATISH CHANDRA SHARMA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Issue arose as regards the applications for condonation of delay in filing the special leave petition and condonation of delay in re-filing the same. Headnotes&dagger; Limitation Act, 1963 &ndash; Condonation of delay of the School filed application for release of grant-in-aid &ndash; Tribunal allowed the application by directing the State and the Director to release grant-in-aid in favour of the teaching and non-teaching staff of the school &ndash; State filed appeal which was time-barred as also not<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 09-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> DIARYNO AND DIARYYR No. 54941/2025</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('6','2026','2026_3_103_112','2026INSC148','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('6','2026','2026_3_